WEBVTT

00:00:13.474 --> 00:00:15.345
ARTHUR:Harry!

00:00:19.915 --> 00:00:22.265
[SPELLS BLASTING]

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.099
Ginny!

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.174
Molly.

00:01:24.022 --> 00:01:26.242
HERMIONE:
It's easy for them
to get to you.

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:28.201
You're bloody lucky
you weren't killed.

00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:30.159
You have to realize
who you are, Harry.

00:01:30.203 --> 00:01:33.641
I know who I am,
Hermione, all right?

00:01:33.684 --> 00:01:35.033
Sorry.

00:01:36.557 --> 00:01:40.038
Lav, come on.
Of course I'll wear it.

00:01:40.082 --> 00:01:42.345
That's my Won-Won.

00:01:43.781 --> 00:01:46.088
Excuse me,
I have to go and vomit.

00:01:51.006 --> 00:01:52.921
[GIGGLING]

00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:06.717
SLUGHORN:
I'd like to know where
you get your information.

00:02:06.761 --> 00:02:09.938
More knowledgeable
than half the staff, you are.

00:02:15.422 --> 00:02:17.380
Sir.

00:02:17.424 --> 00:02:20.383
is it true that Professor
Merrythought is retiring?

00:02:20.427 --> 00:02:23.299
Now, Tom. I couldn't tell
you if I knew, could I?

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.649
By the way,
thank you for the pineapple.

00:02:25.693 --> 00:02:28.130
You're quite right,
it is my favorite.

00:02:28.173 --> 00:02:29.174
But how did you know?

00:02:32.482 --> 00:02:34.615
Intuition.

00:02:36.312 --> 00:02:37.487
[CLOCK CHIMING]

00:02:37.531 --> 00:02:39.576
Gracious.
Is it that time already?

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:41.143
Off you go, boys,

00:02:41.186 --> 00:02:43.058
or Professor Dippet
will have us all in detention.

00:02:44.886 --> 00:02:45.887
[DINGS]

00:02:47.802 --> 00:02:49.586
Look sharp, Tom.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.762
Don't want to be caught
out of bed after hours.

00:02:53.547 --> 00:02:55.766
Is something on your mind, Tom?Yes, sir.

00:02:57.028 --> 00:03:00.684
You see, I couldn't think
of anyone else to go to.

00:03:00.728 --> 00:03:05.820
The other professors,
well, they're not like you.

00:03:05.863 --> 00:03:09.302
They might misunderstand.

00:03:09.345 --> 00:03:11.652
Go on.

00:03:11.695 --> 00:03:14.481
I was in the library
the other night

00:03:14.524 --> 00:03:18.267
in the Restricted Section
and I read something

00:03:18.311 --> 00:03:21.923
rather odd about a bit
of rare magic,

00:03:21.966 --> 00:03:25.579
And I thought perhaps
you could illuminate me.

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:28.538
It's called,
as I understand it...

00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:31.324
[RIDDLE SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY]

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:32.629
I beg your pardon?

00:03:32.673 --> 00:03:34.675
I don't know anything
about such things,

00:03:34.718 --> 00:03:36.546
and if I did,
I wouldn't tell you.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.374
Now, get out of here at once,

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.681
and don't let me ever catch
you mentioning it again!

00:03:44.206 --> 00:03:45.425
DUMBLEDORE:
Confused?

00:03:45.468 --> 00:03:47.644
I'd be surprised if you weren't.

00:03:47.688 --> 00:03:52.432
Well, I don't understand.
What happened?

00:03:52.475 --> 00:03:55.348
This is perhaps the most
important memory I've collected.

00:03:55.391 --> 00:03:57.219
It is also a lie.

00:03:57.262 --> 00:04:00.570
This memory has been
tampered with

00:04:00.614 --> 00:04:02.398
by the same person
whose memory it is,

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.487
our old friend,
Professor Slughorn.

00:04:04.531 --> 00:04:07.447
But why would he tamper
with his own memory?

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:10.188
I suspect he's ashamed of it.Why?

00:04:10.232 --> 00:04:11.799
Why, indeed?

00:04:11.842 --> 00:04:14.715
I asked you to get to know
Professor Slughorn,

00:04:14.758 --> 00:04:16.456
and you have done so.

00:04:16.499 --> 00:04:19.850
Now I want you to persuade him
to divulge his true memory

00:04:19.894 --> 00:04:21.504
any way you can.

00:04:21.548 --> 00:04:23.637
I don't know him
that well, sir.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.079
This memory is everything.

00:04:31.122 --> 00:04:33.908
Without it, we are blind.

00:04:33.951 --> 00:04:36.911
Without it, we leave the fate
of our world to chance.

00:04:39.653 --> 00:04:40.915
You have no choice.

00:04:42.612 --> 00:04:44.135
You must not fail.

00:04:52.361 --> 00:04:54.929
SLUGHORN:
So I'd highly recommend
you reacquaint yourself

00:04:54.972 --> 00:04:56.757
with the chapter on antidotes.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.324
I'll tell you more about bezoars
in our next class.

00:04:59.368 --> 00:05:01.239
Right, off you go.

00:05:01.283 --> 00:05:03.024
Alys, don't forget
your rat tail.

00:05:08.421 --> 00:05:12.337
Aha. If it isn't
the Prince of Potions himself.

00:05:12.381 --> 00:05:14.731
To what do I owe this pleasure?

00:05:16.124 --> 00:05:17.952
Sir, I wondered
if I might ask you something.

00:05:17.995 --> 00:05:20.433
Ask away, dear boy, ask away.

00:05:20.476 --> 00:05:22.173
The other day I was
in the library,

00:05:22.217 --> 00:05:23.871
in the Restricted Section

00:05:23.914 --> 00:05:25.742
and I came across
something rather odd

00:05:25.786 --> 00:05:27.440
about a very rare
piece of magic.

00:05:28.615 --> 00:05:30.921
Yes, and what was this
rare piece of magic?

00:05:30.965 --> 00:05:32.096
Well, I don't know.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.925
I-I can't remember
the name exactly.

00:05:34.969 --> 00:05:37.450
It got me wondering,
are there some kinds of magic

00:05:37.493 --> 00:05:39.452
you're not allowed to teach us?

00:05:41.323 --> 00:05:43.064
I'm Potions Master, Harry.

00:05:43.107 --> 00:05:45.762
I think your question'd better
be posed to Professor Snape.

00:05:45.806 --> 00:05:47.851
Yes. Um...

00:05:47.895 --> 00:05:50.506
He and I don't exactly
see eye to eye, sir.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:53.161
What I mean to say is,

00:05:53.204 --> 00:05:55.206
well, he's not like you.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.600
He might misunderstand.

00:05:58.819 --> 00:06:02.736
Yes. There can be no light
without the dark.

00:06:02.779 --> 00:06:04.302
And so it is with magic.

00:06:04.346 --> 00:06:07.436
Myself, I always strive
to live within the light.

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:09.220
I suggest you do the same.

00:06:09.264 --> 00:06:11.135
Is that what you
told Tom Riddle, sir,

00:06:11.179 --> 00:06:12.659
when he came asking questions?

00:06:18.403 --> 00:06:22.669
Dumbledore put you up to this,
didn't he?

00:06:24.409 --> 00:06:26.281
Didn't he?

00:06:31.547 --> 00:06:32.679
[KNOCKING]

00:06:32.722 --> 00:06:35.725
Yes?

00:06:35.769 --> 00:06:37.422
Oh, it's you, Potter.

00:06:37.466 --> 00:06:39.990
I'm-- I'm sorry,
I'm busy at the moment.

00:06:40.034 --> 00:06:42.079
[LOCK CLICKING]

